{'k':'R3','ti':'Reading Part 3','ins':'Metni oku ve soruları cevapla.','title':'My first job',
 'p':['When I was seventeen, I got a summer job at a small hotel by the sea. I had never worked before, and to be honest, I was more interested in the beach than in the money. My parents thought it would be good for me to learn what work was really like.',
  'On my first day, the manager, Mrs Grant, gave me a uniform that was far too big and asked me to clean twenty rooms before lunch. I thought it was impossible. By twelve o\'clock I had finished only eight, and I was sure she would be angry. Instead, she sat down with me and showed me a better way to organise my work. "Everyone is slow at the beginning," she said.',
  'After a few weeks, I was much faster, and I started to enjoy talking to the guests. Some of them came back every year and told me stories about the hotel in the past. I also made friends with the other young workers, and we often went swimming together after work.',
  'Looking back, I realise that job taught me more than any school lesson. I learned to be patient, to ask for help when I needed it, and to be proud of doing something well. I still use those lessons today in my job as a teacher.'],
 'q':[
  {'q':'Why did the writer take the job?','o':['He needed money for university.','His parents encouraged him to work.','He wanted to live near the beach.','A friend already worked at the hotel.'],'a':1,'tg':['detail'],'e':'"My parents thought it would be good for me" – ailesi teşvik etti.'},
  {'q':'How did the writer feel at twelve o\'clock on his first day?','o':['pleased that he had finished so many rooms','angry with the manager','worried about the manager\'s reaction','bored with the work'],'a':2,'tg':['inference','past-perfect'],'e':'"I was sure she would be angry" – yöneticinin tepkisinden endişe ediyordu.'},
  {'q':'What did Mrs Grant do?','o':['She gave him an easier job.','She explained how to work more efficiently.','She told him to finish the rooms after lunch.','She gave him a smaller uniform.'],'a':1,'tg':['detail'],'e':'"showed me a better way to organise my work" = daha verimli çalışmayı gösterdi.'},
  {'q':'What did the writer enjoy most after a few weeks?','o':['swimming alone','the guests\' stories','cleaning the rooms quickly','working extra hours'],'a':1,'tg':['detail'],'e':'Misafirlerle konuşmayı ve onların otelin geçmişiyle ilgili hikâyelerini sevdi.'},
  {'q':'What is the writer\'s main point in the text?','o':['Hotel work is too difficult for young people.','Teachers should have experience of working in other jobs first.','His first job taught him important lessons for life.','Managers should be kind to new workers.'],'a':2,'tg':['gist'],'e':'Son paragraf: o iş ona okul derslerinden daha çok şey öğretti.'},
 ]},

{'k':'R4','ti':'Reading Part 4','ins':'Metinden beş cümle çıkarıldı. Her boşluk için uygun cümleyi (A–H) seç. Üç cümle fazladır.','title':'The town that gave up cars',
 'p':'Ten years ago, the small town of Lindhaven decided to close its centre to cars. Many shop owners were against the idea. (1) ______ They were worried that customers would stop coming.\nIn the first few months, things were difficult. Some shops did lose business. (2) ______ People began to walk and cycle into town, and they stayed longer because the streets were quieter and cleaner.\nThe town also built a large car park just outside the centre. (3) ______ The bus is free, so people do not mind leaving their cars there.\nToday, Lindhaven has more shops than before. (4) ______ Visitors from other countries come to see how the town changed.\nNot everyone is happy, of course. Older people sometimes find it hard to carry heavy shopping a long way. (5) ______ It seems that most problems can be solved if people are willing to talk.',
 's':[('A','But after a year, the situation started to change.'),('B','From there, a small bus takes visitors to the main square every ten minutes.'),('C','They believed that people would not want to walk.'),('D','The town plans to open the centre to cars again next year.'),('E','To help them, the town now offers a free delivery service.'),('F','Many of them are cafés with tables outside in the street.'),('G','The bus stopped running because nobody used it.'),('H','Cars are much cheaper to use in the countryside.')],
 'a':['C','A','B','F','E'],'tg':['coherence','coherence','reference','coherence','reference'],
 'e':['"They were worried..." öncesinde dükkân sahiplerinin düşüncesi gelmeli: C.','"did lose business" sonrası "But after a year" ile değişim başlıyor: A.','"From there" = otoparktan; sonraki cümlede "The bus is free": B.','Daha çok dükkân → "Many of them are cafés": F.','Yaşlıların zorluğuna çözüm: "To help them": E.']},

{'k':'R5','ti':'Reading Part 5','ins':'Metni oku ve her boşluk için doğru kelimeyi seç.','title':'A weekend in the mountains',
 'p':'Last weekend my family and I (1) ______ on a trip to the mountains. We had booked a small cabin (2) ______ was next to a lake. On Saturday we got up early and (3) ______ a long walk through the forest. It was quite (4) ______, but the views from the top were amazing. In the evening it started to rain, so we stayed inside and played cards. We enjoyed it so much (5) ______ we have already decided to go back next year. I would (6) ______ it to anyone who loves nature.',
 'o':[(['went','made','did','took'],0,['vocab']),(['who','which','where','what'],1,['relative-clauses']),(['went','made','took','did'],2,['vocab']),(['tiring','tired','tire','tiredness'],0,['vocab']),(['because','that','so','than'],1,['linkers-contrast-purpose']),(['advise','recommend','tell','say'],1,['reporting-verbs'])],
 'e':['go on a trip: geziye çıkmak.','Şey (cabin) için which; arkasından fiil geliyor.','take a walk: yürüyüşe çıkmak.','Yürüyüş yorucuydu: tiring (yorucu). tired = yorgun (kişi).','so ... that: o kadar ... ki.','recommend something to someone: birine bir şeyi tavsiye etmek. advise ve tell bu kalıpla kullanılmaz.']},

{'k':'R6','ti':'Reading Part 6','ins':'Metni oku ve her boşluğa TEK kelime yaz.','title':'Hi Jess!',
 'p':'Hi Jess!\nI\'m writing (1) ______ tell you about my new school. I started here two weeks ago and I really like it. The teachers are very friendly and there are lots of clubs. I\'ve already joined the drama club, (2) ______ meets every Wednesday. My best friend here is called Mia. She lives (3) ______ the same street as me, so we walk to school together. The only problem is that the school is (4) ______ bigger than my old one, and I sometimes get lost! Have you ever (5) ______ to a new school? Write back soon and tell me (6) ______ you are doing.\nLove, Ella',
 'a':[['to'],['which'],['on','in'],['much','far','a lot'],['been','gone','moved','changed'],['how','what']],
 'tg':[['gerund-infinitive'],['relative-clauses'],['prepositions-in-on-at'],['comparatives-superlatives'],['present-perfect'],['reported-speech']],
 'e':['Amaç: to + fiil (I\'m writing to tell you).','Virgüllü ek bilgi, şey (club): which.','Sokak adıyla on (İngiltere\'de in de kullanılır).','Karşılaştırmayı güçlendirme: much / far / a lot bigger.','Have you ever been to ...? deneyim sorusu (moved / changed da anlamca kabul edilir).','Dolaylı soru: tell me how you are doing (what you are doing da olur).']},

